Proposed Dr Johnson’s Detangling Hair Conditioner — Product Specification

Purpose
A rinse-out conditioner designed to improve hair slip, reduce tangling, and make wet and dry hair easier to comb. Intended to improve manageability and the appearance of fullness; no hair-growth claim.

Feature

Proposed requirement

Product form

Smooth, pourable combable conditioning lotion

Pack size

500 ml

Packaging

Clearly labelled bottle with controlled dispensing

Intended users

Adults; children’s suitability requires separate assessment

Hair types

Normal, dry, and tangle-prone hair

Finish

Soft, manageable hair with minimal greasy residue

Fragrance

Light fragrance, with a fragrance-free option

Application

Apply after shampooing, distribute through lengths and ends, then rinse thoroughly

Formulation brief
Develop a cosmetic-grade, water-based emulsion containing a suitable conditioning agent for detangling, fatty alcohols for slip and texture, and a balanced amount of emollient to soften hair without weighing it down. Include a compatible preservative system and adjust pH to suit the finished formulation.

Ingredient selection, concentrations, and manufacturing instructions must be developed by a qualified cosmetic formulator.

Performance targets

Reduce wet-combing force compared with shampoo alone.

Improve dry combability and reduce static and flyaways.

Leave hair feeling soft without an excessively oily coating.

Remain easy to dispense and rinse out.

Validation before sale
Confirm safety, preservative effectiveness, stability, packaging compatibility, and performance. Support any “easier combing,” “less breakage,” or “fuller-looking hair” claims with appropriate testing.

Suggested label description
“A lightweight rinse-out conditioner that helps detangle and soften hair, leaving it smoother, more manageable, and easier to comb.”
